          Meesho Supplier Panel Guide &bull; 2026 Edition
        </span>
        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-neutral-900 mt-3">
          The Complete Meesho Seller Calculator &amp; Meesho Price Calculator: Zero Commission Economics, Returns &amp; Payouts
        </h2>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-neutral-500 mt-2 font-mono">
          Learn how to master Meesho pricing, dead weight shipping slabs, customer return reserves, and true take-home profits.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Introduction -->
      <p>
        Meesho has transformed Indian e-commerce by introducing a revolutionary 0% commission marketplace model designed specifically for value-conscious shoppers across Tier 2, Tier 3, and rural India. For manufacturers, wholesalers, and direct-to-consumer merchants, selling on Meesho offers an unprecedented opportunity to move high inventory volumes without paying the standard 10% to 20% platform commissions charged by traditional marketplaces. However, running a profitable business on Meesho requires navigating a unique operational reality. Using a dedicated <strong>meesho seller calculator</strong> alongside our <a href="/" class="text-emerald-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-900 font-medium">multi-marketplace seller profit calculator</a> is critical for achieving consistent profitability.
      </p>

      <p>
        Because Meesho shoppers are extremely price-sensitive, retail margins are compressed. Furthermore, Indian Cash on Delivery (COD) logistics carry return hazards that can easily wipe out your profits if left uncalculated. By using our free <a href="/selling-price-calculator/" class="text-emerald-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-900 font-medium">product pricing calculator</a> and seller suite, suppliers can model exact courier freight slabs, customer return penalty buffers, and tax withholdings. This guide explains how the <strong>meesho commission calculator</strong> works, how to structure optimal <strong>meesho pricing</strong>, and how top sellers build profitable multi-crore businesses on the platform.
      </p>

      <!-- H3: The 0% Commission Policy -->
      <h3 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 pt-2 border-t border-neutral-100">
        The Truth About Meesho Commission: Zero Percent Myth vs Reality
      </h3>
      <p>
        When sellers first explore a <strong>meesho commission calculator</strong>, the most striking feature is the complete absence of referral commissions and fixed closing fees. Across almost all product categories (fashion, home, beauty, accessories, footwear):
      </p>

      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-neutral-600">
        <li><strong>Referral Commission:</strong> Exactly 0% across all catalog listings.</li>
        <li><strong>Fixed / Closing Fee:</strong> ₹0 per delivered shipment.</li>
        <li><strong>Payment Gateway Fee:</strong> ₹0 on both online prepaid UPI payments and Cash on Delivery orders.</li>
        <li><strong>Listing &amp; Subscription Fees:</strong> Free to list products with no monthly recurring seller account maintenance charges.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        When compared against other channels using our <a href="/amazon-profit-calculator/" class="text-emerald-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-900 font-medium">Amazon profit calculator</a> and <a href="/flipkart-profit-calculator/" class="text-emerald-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-900 font-medium">Flipkart profit calculator</a>, Meesho appears to offer instant 12% to 18% margin savings. However, smart sellers understand that Meesho’s zero-commission model shifts the primary expense from platform commissions to shipping logistics and customer return buffers.
      </p>

      <!-- H3: Meesho Logistics and Courier Dead Weight Slabs -->
      <h3 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 pt-2 border-t border-neutral-100">
        Meesho Logistics &amp; Shipping Charges: How Dead Weight Works
      </h3>
      <p>
        Unlike marketplaces that enforce complex volumetric calculations, Meesho primarily bills shipping based on physical dead weight in 500g slabs:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-neutral-600">
        <li><strong>Local Delivery (&le; 500g):</strong> Typically ₹45 to ₹52.</li>
        <li><strong>Regional Delivery (&le; 500g):</strong> Typically ₹52 to ₹60.</li>
        <li><strong>National Delivery (&le; 500g):</strong> Typically ₹62 to ₹72.</li>
        <li><strong>Additional 500g Increments:</strong> +₹25 to +₹35 per incremental slab.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        To prevent shipping discrepancies, verify your parcel brackets on our <a href="/courier-charges-calculator/" class="text-emerald-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-900 font-medium">courier charges calculator</a> and compare third-party courier aggregators using our <a href="/shipping-cost-calculator/" class="text-emerald-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-900 font-medium">shipping cost calculator</a>.
      </p>

      <!-- H3: Real Unit Economics Breakdown -->
