      <!-- H3: RTO and Customer Return Realities -->
      <h3 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 pt-2 border-t border-neutral-100">
        Mastering Returns: RTO vs Customer Returns on Meesho
      </h3>
      <p>
        Because Meesho caters to Tier 2 and Tier 3 shoppers with high COD adoption, return rates can reach 25% to 35% in fashion and footwear. Managing returns effectively is what separates thriving Meesho suppliers from those who suffer catastrophic losses:
      </p>
      <ol class="list-decimal pl-5 space-y-2 text-neutral-600">
        <li><strong>Zero Penalty on RTOs:</strong> If a customer cancels before delivery or rejects the parcel at the doorstep, Meesho does not levy return freight penalties on the seller. The parcel returns to your warehouse without additional reverse shipping charges. However, you still lose forward packaging costs and capital turnover speed.</li>
        <li><strong>Customer Return Penalties:</strong> If the buyer accepts the parcel, opens it, and initiates a return within 7 days, Meesho charges reverse courier shipping (typically ₹120 to ₹160 per item). Furthermore, customer-returned stock often incurs damage or missing tags.</li>
        <li><strong>Maintain Adequate Profit Margins:</strong> Always verify that your target price provides an adequate cash buffer using our <a href="/profit-margin-calculator/" class="text-emerald-700 underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-emerald-900 font-medium">profit margin calculator</a> before going live.</li>
      </ol>

      <!-- H3: Sourcing and Fulfillment Strategy -->
      <h3 class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-bold text-neutral-900 pt-2 border-t border-neutral-100">
        Sourcing &amp; Tax Compliance for Meesho Suppliers
      </h3>
      <p>
        To build a sustainable multi-channel e-commerce operation, combine Meesho’s high inventory turnover with disciplined procurement and statutory compliance:
      </p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-1.5 text-neutral-600">
